/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (For my Gearshift transmission, before on deciding what ratios to even use, I had to see what ratios were possible out of a planetary gear set. This was for space constraints, and I also wanted to see if a planetary gear ratio, holding the carrier, could have an output ratio of 2:1. As shown below, it is impossible \(the blue graph\). Although it does asymptote towards it as the sun gear gets much much larger than the planet gear. The graph is plotted as number of teeth of each gear \(the sun and planet are usually the gears which you design first\) with the z axis being the output ratio.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
