/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Now, instead of having an input force, we can describe T_in as F_in x r_in, and have an input torque. In order to keep the mathematical ratio of F_out to T_in, if we turn F_out into T_out by multiplying it by r_out, we must also divide by r_out.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
518 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Eventually, the ratio of input torque to output force can be described purely with the geometry of the system: the radii of the gears, compared with the radius of the output lever.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [19]
>>
