539 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Think of it this way: The screw and nut are so tight, that they prevent the inner race from moving. However, the outer race is still free to move. And because it is embedded into the piece, the piece is also able to freely move around the bearing.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [8]
>>
